MAME FM: the phase modulation without shifting a negative number

op_calc() scales the phase modulation by 32768 with a left shift, and the
modulation is signed. The shift of a negative number is undefined behaviour,
and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program at it:

  src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c:1664:69: runtime error: left shift of
  negative value -376

A multiplication says the same thing and is defined. The sum it feeds is
worked out in an unsigned type, as before, so nothing else about the
expression changes. The YM2612 and the YM2608 cores have the same line.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c b/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c
index 6af76a1..4ac3de0 100644
--- a/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c
+++ b/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c
@@ -1661,7 +1661,7 @@ INLINE signed int op_calc(UINT32 phase, unsigned int env, signed int pm)
 {
   UINT32 p;
 
-  p = (env<<3) + sin_tab[ ( ((signed int)((phase & ~FREQ_MASK) + (pm<<15))) >> FREQ_SH ) & SIN_MASK ];
+  p = (env<<3) + sin_tab[ ( ((signed int)((phase & ~FREQ_MASK) + (pm * 32768))) >> FREQ_SH ) & SIN_MASK ];
 
   if (p >= TL_TAB_LEN)
     return 0;
diff --git a/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp b/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp
index fa9b16e..3fda9f1 100644
--- a/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp
+++ b/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp
@@ -1095,7 +1095,7 @@ static inline signed int op_calc(uint32_t phase, unsigned int env, signed int pm
 {
 	uint32_t p;
 
-	p = (env<<3) + sin_tab[ ( ((signed int)((phase & ~FREQ_MASK) + (pm<<15))) >> FREQ_SH ) & SIN_MASK ];
+	p = (env<<3) + sin_tab[ ( ((signed int)((phase & ~FREQ_MASK) + (pm * 32768))) >> FREQ_SH ) & SIN_MASK ];
 
 	if (p >= TL_TAB_LEN)
 		return 0;
